// Spread and read, the second of the paper's three opening programs, with the
// automatic forget: allocate |0>, apply a Hadamard, let the temporary control
// an X on the visible register, then discard it.  The two are entangled and
// the criterion of this work refuses the drop.  The question here is what the
// automatic forget does with the same program.
def main(){
	t := H(0:𝔹);
	x := 0:𝔹;
	if t { x := X(x); }   // x := x + t: t reads into x
	forget(t);
	return measure(x);
}
